        "raw": "<p>Ok, the question that I have is very fundamental, and that fact that no one has asked yet makes me think I&#39;m just missing it in the rule book.</p><p>How many times can a player use a given action during Go Time!? &nbsp;The only thing I can find in the rule book is &quot;During your Go Time! phase, you may use one or more of your actions to do one or more of these:&quot; &nbsp;This seems to imply that I could Sprint three times if I wanted to. &nbsp;It certainly does not give me the impression that I can use each action only once. &nbsp;And yet there are several small things that suggest that you can do each action only once per turn. &nbsp;Like under Sprint where is says &quot;Because Move and Sprint are separate actions, you may do both in the same turn.&quot; &nbsp;Also, Unlimited makes no sense unless you can do each power only once.</p><p>Where is this in the rule book?</p>",
